activity-description.narrative:
ADA campaign alluding to October 1st, International Day of Older Persons;
Creation and training of Community Self-Help Groups (CSOs) involving relevant stakeholders in adaptable and shock-sensitive social protection systems;
Data collection (Assistance to CSOs)

Creation and training of 4 new Community Support Organizations (CSOs) and self-help groups in various communities;

Training of paralegals and strengthening of mechanisms for referring cases of violence against older people;

Implementation of income-generating activities, including pig and chicken farming and charcoal sales;

Implementation and monitoring of savings groups with financial education and revolving credit;

Celebration of the International Day of Older Persons, with cultural activities, provision of compensation and social awareness campaigns;

Institutional meetings with INAS (National Institute for Social Action) to discuss the digital transition of social payments and the need to create a joint technical team;

Conducting home visits to vulnerable families and collecting community data, which reinforce the importance of the intervention.
